  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Living Territories: small scale farmers&apos; defence against extractivism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to consolidate the defence of rural territories in the context of the expansion of legal mining in Colombia. It will be implemented between 2026 and 2028 in Cajamarca (Tolima) and El Carmen de Atrato (Choc&#xf3;), with the participation of local organisations such as COSAJUCA, the Cajamarca Environmental and Small Scale Farming Committee and Anaime, the Peasant Platform and the Social and Environmental Roundtable of El Carmen de Atrato.
Through three lines of action&#x2014;legal enforceability, organisational strengthening and political advocacy&#x2014;the aim is to guarantee the rights of small scale farmers in the face of mining projects, strengthen them as political actors and transform the legal frameworks that regulate the extractive model.</narrative>
  </description>
